epo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"### Crash on Android 6 (API 23)\r\nI think we have to give up support for API < 24 here as well, like in Godot 4.x\r\n\r\n\r\n`java.lang.UnsatisfiedLinkError: dlopen failed: cannot locate symbol \"in6addr_any\" referenced by \"/data/app/org.godotengine.firstgodotproject-1/lib/arm/libgodot_android.so\"...`\r\n\r\n----------------\r\n`v3.6.1.stable.official [b1ba98fce]`\r\n\r\n```\r\nwith custom template: \r\n`Godot Engine v3.7.dev.custom_build.ecb6f7aa2`\r\n\r\n1) Android 13,  arm64, OpenGL ES 2.0 Renderer: Adreno (TM) 650\r\n2) Android 8.1, arm64, OpenGL ES 2.0 Renderer: Adreno (TM) 418\r\n3) Android 8.1, arm32, OpenGL ES 2.0 Renderer: Mali-T830\r\n\r\n4) Android 6,   arm32, Adreno 3xx (CRASH)\r\n\r\nOK with '3.6.1' template:\r\nGodot Engine v3.6.1.stable.official.b1ba98fce\r\nOpenGL ES 2.0 Renderer: Adreno (TM) 320\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n```\r\n<details><summary>crash log</summary>\r\n\r\n```java\r\n--------- beginning of crash\r\n08-07 22:25:35.256  3011  3011 E AndroidRuntime: FATAL EXCEPTION: main\r\n08-07 22:25:35.256  3011  3011 E AndroidRuntime: Process: org.godotengine.firstgodotproject, PID: 3011\r\n08-07 22:25:35.256  3011  3011 E AndroidRuntime: java.lang.UnsatisfiedLinkError: dlopen failed: cannot locate symbol \"in6addr_any\" referenced by \"/data/app/org.godotengine.firstgodotproject-1/lib/arm/libgodot_android.so\"...\r\n08-07 22:25:35.256  3011  3011 E AndroidRuntime: \tat java.lang.Runtime.loadLibrary(Runtime.java:372)\r\n08-07 22:25:35.256  3011  3011 E AndroidRuntime: \tat java.lang.System.loadLibrary(System.java:1076)\r\n08-07 22:25:35.256  3011  3011 E AndroidRuntime: \tat org.godotengine.godot.GodotLib.<clinit>(GodotLib.java:50)\r\n08-07 22:25:35.256  3011  3011 E AndroidRuntime: \tat org.godotengine.godot.Godot.initializeGodot(Godot.java:695)\r\n08-07 22:25:35.256  3011  3011 E AndroidRuntime: \tat org.godotengine.godot.Godot.onCreate(Godot.java:844)\r\n08-07 22:25:35.256  3011  3011 E AndroidRuntime: \tat androidx.fragment.app.Fragment.performCreate(Fragment.java:3099)\r\n08-07 22:25:35.256  3011  3011 E AndroidRuntime: \tat androidx.fragment.app.FragmentStateManager.create(FragmentStateManager.java:524)\r\n08-07 22:25:35.256  3011  3011 E AndroidRuntime: \tat androidx.fragment.app.FragmentStateManager.moveToExpectedState(FragmentStateManager.java:282)\r\n08-07 22:25:35.256  3011  3011 E AndroidRuntime: \tat androidx.fragment.app.FragmentManager.executeOpsTogether(FragmentManager.java:2214)\r\n08-07 22:25:35.256  3011  3011 E AndroidRuntime: \tat androidx.fragment.app.FragmentManager.removeRedundantOperationsAndExecute(FragmentManager.java:2109)\r\n08-07 22:25:35.256  3011  3011 E AndroidRuntime: \tat androidx.fragment.app.FragmentManager.execSingleAction(FragmentManager.java:2002)\r\n08-07 22:25:35.256  3011  3011 E AndroidRuntime: \tat androidx.fragment.app.BackStackRecord.commitNowAllowingStateLoss(BackStackRecord.java:323)\r\n08-07 22:25:35.256  3011  3011 E AndroidRuntime: \tat org.godotengine.godot.FullScreenGodotApp.onCreate(FullScreenGodotApp.java:74)\r\n\r\n```\r\n</details>\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/1f4dce03b2d51fcc0a49caf7f95cb3e188f0b962/drivers/unix/net_socket_posix.cpp#L98-L112\r\n\r\n------------\r\n\r\nmaybe possible solution:\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\n#if __ANDROID_API__ < 24\r\nconst struct in6_addr my_in6addr_any = IN6ADDR_ANY_INIT;\r\n#define in6addr_any my_in6addr_any\r\n#endif\r\n```\r\nBut it is very likely that more similar workarounds are necessary.\r\n\r\n@m4gr3d what is your opinion on this?\r\n\r\n","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengin